{{!--
  This app is deployed separately, on its own hostname, and sets its own
  session cookie — so it needs its own notice rather than pointing at the
  platform's. Keep the table in step with what src/server.js actually sets.
--}}
<section class="container-fluid py-4 px-lg-5">
  <div class="mb-4">
    <p class="eyebrow">Cookies</p>
    <h1 class="mb-1">Cookies and local storage</h1>
    <p class="text-muted mb-0" style="max-width: 70ch">
      This app sets no analytics, advertising or tracking cookies, and no third
      party sets a cookie through it. Everything below is needed for it to work,
      which is why you are told about it rather than asked to agree to it.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="surface-card">
    <div class="table-responsive">
      <table class="table align-middle mb-0">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Name</th>
            <th scope="col">Set by</th>
            <th scope="col">What it does</th>
            <th scope="col">How long</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><code>expenses.sid</code></td>
            <td>This app</td>
            <td>
              Keeps you signed in after you approve the wallet challenge. It is
              only set once you start signing in &mdash; browsing the landing
              pages sets no session cookie at all.
            </td>
            <td>Until you sign out or close the browser</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>ARRAffinity</code><br><code>ARRAffinitySameSite</code></td>
            <td>Our host, Azure App Service</td>
            <td>
              Keeps you on the same server for the length of a visit, so a
              request does not land on a machine that has never heard of your
              session.
            </td>
            <td>Until you close the browser</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>aegis.cookie-notice</code></td>
            <td>This app</td>
            <td>
              Remembers that you have read the notice at the bottom of the page.
              Stored on your device by the browser, never sent to us.
            </td>
            <td>Until you clear it</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="row g-4 mt-1">
    <div class="col-lg-4">
      <div class="surface-card h-100">
        <h2 class="h5">If you block them</h2>
        <p class="text-muted mb-0">
          You can clear or block any of this in your browser, and nothing here
          works around that. Blocking the session cookie means you cannot sign
          in, because it is the thing that remembers you are signed in. No other
          feature changes.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="col-lg-4">
      <div class="surface-card h-100">
        <h2 class="h5">Why there is no Accept or Decline</h2>
        <p class="text-muted mb-0">
          Consent is for storage that is not strictly necessary &mdash;
          analytics, advertising, anything that builds a profile. This app runs
          none of it, so there is nothing you could decline.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="col-lg-4">
      <div class="surface-card h-100">
        <h2 class="h5">Signing in with Aegis ID</h2>
        <p class="text-muted mb-0">
          Signing in sends you to {{aegisBaseUrl}}, which is a separate site with
          its own cookies and its own notice. Nothing about you is shared with a
          third party by either.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
